# Pairs with RestoreConverges, under the fairness Spec asserts. A receive-gate
# cache that re-reads the fence but keeps the epoch it first read stamps every
# later admission with a pre-restore epoch, so the restored copy refuses every
# post-cutover write for good and the clusters never converge. Its code analogue
# (the cache dropping the epoch) turns ReplicationReceiveGateTests red.
MODULE: RestoreConvergesGateCacheKeepsStaleEpoch
TARGET: RestoreConverges
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: the receive-gate cache never refreshes the epoch it stamps
PERTURBS: Refresh

--- FIND
    /\ seen' = [seen EXCEPT ![c] = [open |-> recvOn[c], ep |-> epoch[c]]]
--- REPLACE
    \* MUTATION: the cached epoch is never refreshed.
    /\ seen' = [seen EXCEPT ![c] = [open |-> recvOn[c], ep |-> seen[c].ep]]
--- END
